Add a model-level leaderboard; swap the hero nav links

Hero drops Results and Failure cases in favour of Overview (anchored on
the existing Motivation section) and Leaderboard.

The leaderboard reports one row per model rather than per configuration.
Where a model ran under several settings, only its best paired pass rate
is listed and the configuration is named beside it: Gemini Live 2.5
Flash keeps proactive (7.5 over 7.4) and GPT-Realtime keeps VAD (2.7
over 1.9). That takes 15 configurations down to 13 models. Table 1 still
carries every configuration.

The -RL variants stay as separate rows. Interaction RL post-training
produces different weights rather than a different inference setting, so
Moshi/Moshi-RL and PersonaPlex/PersonaPlex-RL are not the same model
under two configs.

Styling follows the ihbench leaderboard: sortable columns, family colour
dots, inline proportional bars with the number at the end, and a
segmented All / Closed-source / Open-weight filter. Second metric is the
per-instruction average from Figure 4, which mostly reflects default
behaviour rather than instruction following.

